      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "At t=1, (x',y')=(-1,4), speed=√17, (x'',y'')=(2,2), acceleration magnitude=2√2, and position=(-1,3); only option 3 is false."
    },
    {
      "qid": 4,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|4",
      "sourceOrdinal": 4,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "⑤",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f'=e^x-1 changes from negative to positive at x=0; values at -3,0,1 are e^-3+3, 1, e-1, so max=e^-3+3 and min=1."
    },
    {
      "qid": 5,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|5",
      "sourceOrdinal": 5,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "tan²x=sec²x-1, hence its antiderivative is tan x-x+C; option 3 has the wrong sign."
    },
    {
      "qid": 6,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|6",
      "sourceOrdinal": 6,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "With u=x², du=2x dx; the integral is 1/2∫_0^4 e^u du = (e^4-1)/2."
    },
    {
      "qid": 7,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|7",
      "sourceOrdinal": 7,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "④",
      "decisiveCalculation": "An antiderivative is F(x)=2x²lnx-x²+xlnx-x. F(e)-F(1)=e²+2, so f(e)=2+(e²+2)=e²+4."
    },
    {
      "qid": 8,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|8",
      "sourceOrdinal": 8,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "This is the right-endpoint Riemann sum for ∫_0^1 x^4 dx=1/5."
    },
    {
      "qid": 9,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|9",
      "sourceOrdinal": 9,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "At tangency x=a the tangent is y-1/a=-(x-a)/a². Passing through (-2,0) gives -a=2+a, so a=-1 and the line is y=-x-2."
    },
    {
      "qid": 10,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|10",
      "sourceOrdinal": 10,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f'(x)=Σ_(k=1)^10 k x^(-k-1); at x=-1 this is 1-2+3-4+…+9-10=-5."
    },
    {
      "qid": 11,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|11",
      "sourceOrdinal": 11,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The limit gives f(6)=3 and f'(6)=1/3. Thus g(3)=6 and g'(3)=1/f'(6)=3; the sum is 9."
    },
    {
      "qid": 12,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|12",
      "sourceOrdinal": 12,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "④",
      "decisiveCalculation": "For y=xe^-x, y''=e^-x(x-2), so A=(2,2/e²); the tangent is y=(4-x)/e² with intercepts B=(4,0), C=(0,4/e²), giving area 8/e²."
    },
    {
      "qid": 13,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|13",
      "sourceOrdinal": 13,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f'=cos x, so f(π/3)-f(π/6)=sin(π/3)-sin(π/6)=(√3-1)/2."
    },
    {
      "qid": 14,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|14",
      "sourceOrdinal": 14,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "Integrating f'=1/[x√(lnx+10)] with u=lnx+10 gives f(e^6)-f(1/e)=2(√16-√9)=2; hence f(e^6)=12."
    },
    {
      "qid": 15,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|15",
      "sourceOrdinal": 15,
      "disposition": "ITEM_HOLD",
      "answer": null,
      "decisiveCalculation": "For x≠0, (f/x)'=3x e^(x²), so f(x)/x=(3/2)e^(x²)+C. From f(1)=0, f(2)=3(e^4-e), which matches none of the five frozen choices; hold only q15."
    },
    {
      "qid": 16,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|16",
      "sourceOrdinal": 16,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "g'(t)=2(t-1)/[(t-1)²+1] is negative for t<1. Opposite directions on exactly (1/4,1) require f'(t)=2t-a>0 there with boundary a/2=1/4, so a=1/2."
    },
    {
      "qid": 17,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|단답형 1",
      "sourceOrdinal": 17,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$11$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The average of e^(kx), k=1,…,10, is 1+(55/10)x+O(x²); its logarithm is (11/2)x+O(x²), and multiplication by 2/x gives 11."
    },
    {
      "qid": 18,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|단답형 2",
      "sourceOrdinal": 18,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$-16$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "dy/dx=(dy/dθ)/(dx/dθ)=-2tanθ; differentiating with respect to x gives d²y/dx²=-2sec³θ, which is -16 at θ=π/3."
    },
    {
      "qid": 19,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|서·논술형 1",
      "sourceOrdinal": 19,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$e^2$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "Differentiate the identity once: f(x)-e^4=∫_0^x f(t)dt. At x=0 this gives f(0)=e^4; differentiating again gives f'=f, so f(x)=e^(x+4) and f(-2)=e²."
    },
    {
      "qid": 20,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|서·논술형 2",
      "sourceOrdinal": 20,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "With u=lnx, a_n=∫_1^0 u^n du=-1/(n+1). Thus a_n a_(n+1)=1/[(n+1)(n+2)]=1/(n+1)-1/(n+2), and the infinite sum is 1/2."
    },
    {
      "qid": 21,
      "questionUid": "sha256:0b4a3e6e1fb32fe42fa43949e26ebc73b42514edaa6bc0e20d23c6d4027cd020|서·논술형 3",
      "sourceOrdinal": 21,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$4$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "From f(1)=e and f'(1)=e, a+b=0 and 2a+b=-2, hence a=-2,b=2 and f'(x)=x²e^x. Since f(1)=e, g(e)=e; differentiating g(f(x))=f'(x) gives g'(e)=f''(1)/f'(1)=3. Also (f^-1)'(e)=1/e, so h'(e)=e/e+3=4."
    }
